WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.670 line:-3
Stop using it like Google.

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:22.220 line:-3
Nearly 1 000 pupils. Practice with AI: +48% and +127%. Exam, AI off: −17%. Practice soared. Learning sank.

3
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:34.830 line:-3
Asked “Are you sure?”, one model wrongly admitted a “mistake” in up to 98% of challenged answers.

4
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:44.750 line:-3
A legal team cited nine cases. Only two could be traced. The court: “irresponsible and downright unprofessional”.

5
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:55.200 line:-3
Asked to explain 36 + 59, it described “carry the one”. That is not what it actually did.

6
00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:05.350 line:-3
Augment your thinking: explain, question, give feedback. Don’t automate it: write, solve, summarise for you.

7
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:16.070 line:-3
Attempt it first. Name the blockage. Ask for ONE hint. Check it. Close the AI, go again.

8
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:25.980 line:-3
The hint ladder: climb only as high as you need. The full solution is the last resort.

9
00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:37.570 line:-3
UCT stopped using AI-detection scores: “simply not reliable”. Expect to explain your work out loud. Declare your AI use.

10
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:50.850 line:-3
Brain On, AI On: AI is a power tool. Your brain is the power. Co-Pilot, Not Autopilot: you fly the plane. AI helps you navigate.

11
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:59.830 line:-3
The measure that counts: what you can do with the AI switched off.
